    section3Body: "Enquiries for professional pagri tying technique for destination weddings generally come from people in one of a few situations: actively finalising wedding vendors with a confirmed date, researching options before anything is locked in, or coordinating on behalf of someone else — a family member, or a professional wedding planner managing a client's full vendor list. We treat all of these the same way at the enquiry stage: share what you know so far, even if it's incomplete, and we'll respond with whatever is useful at that stage, whether that's firm availability and pricing or just general guidance while you're still deciding. Planners working across multiple bookings are welcome to reach out directly without the couple needing to be involved in the initial conversation. If you're helping arrange things for someone else, it's worth including their contact details once a specific package and colour direction needs confirming, since that decision is usually easiest to finalise with the person who'll actually be wearing the safa.",
    section4Title: "What's included and how pricing works",
    section4Body: "The price behind professional pagri tying technique for destination weddings isn't a single fixed figure — it moves with guest count, fabric choice, styling detail and travel distance for bookings outside our core area. What stays consistent across every package is what's actually included: the artist's time, full coordination of the tying order around your ceremony schedule, and attention to fit and finish for every person styled. Fabric itself is either supplied as part of the package or, if your family has already chosen fabric, we quote for tying support only — both are common requests. Accessories such as a kalgi, brooch or pearl detail are generally an optional add-on rather than something bundled into every booking automatically. If you'd like a number to plan around, share your event date, venue, approximate headcount and fabric preference together, and we'll respond with a package that's based on your actual event rather than a generic starting price.",
